    "faqs_about": {
      "type": "custom-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_q01": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What is MUTO NAD+ Cellular Complex?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO NAD+ Cellular Complex is a daily supplement that supports the 30 trillion cells in your body through NAD+ and other nutrients. It’s two capsules with your first meal: 19 ingredients, every dose on the label, made in the UK. And it’s built to be checked. Take a baseline, track the difference in how your days feel or on your wearable, and make your own call, with a 90-day money-back guarantee behind it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q02": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who is MUTO for?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO is for people who are still training, still working and not ready to slow down. Most of our customers are in their 40s and 50s. If your afternoons fade sooner than they used to, sessions take longer to bounce back from, or you’re taking several supplements and don’t know which one’s working, MUTO is built for you. Some customers track HRV or recovery on a wearable; many simply notice how their days feel. MUTO is for adults over 18 only.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q03": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MUTO for women too?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Plenty of our customers are women, and many tell us the first thing they notice is their afternoons. The formula is the same for everyone. If you take any medication, check with your GP or pharmacist first.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q04": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How is MUTO different from other NAD+ supplements?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO is built to be checked, not taken on trust. Most supplements ask you to believe they’re working. We give you a way to find out: every dose declared, a baseline to start from, help reading your own data, and a 90-day guarantee if you don’t see a difference. It’s also a complete daily formula rather than a single ingredient, with nicotinamide riboside (NR) alongside CoQ10, TMG, resveratrol, PQQ, methylated B vitamins, zinc, copper, D3 and K2. <a href=\"/pages/science\">Read the science behind the formula.</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q05": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is NAD+ just hype?",
            "content": "<p>There’s a lot of hype around NAD+, which is exactly why we built MUTO to be checked. The science is real: NAD+ is essential to how every cell makes energy, and 300mg of NR a day has been shown to raise blood NAD+ in human studies. What no one can promise is how any supplement will make you feel. So we don’t ask you to believe it. Note your starting point, give it 90 days, and decide for yourself.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q06": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I check your claims?",
            "content": "<p>Please do. Every ingredient and dose is on the label and on this page. Paste it into ChatGPT, or show it to your GP, pharmacist or nutritionist. Batch certificates are available on request, and Richie answers formula questions himself.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q07": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Who makes MUTO?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO was founded by Dr Richie Barclay, a PhD scientist in cellular biology and nutrition (not a medical doctor), and is formulated with a six-member Scientific Advisory Board. It’s manufactured in the UK to GMP standards in an ISO-certified facility. You can ask us anything about the formula: <a href=\"mailto:hello@mutolongevity.com\">hello@mutolongevity.com</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q08": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MUTO being clinically studied?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. MUTO is part of independent university research programmes, starting with a University of Westminster study in December 2026, followed by work with King’s College London in early 2027 and Coventry and Newcastle universities later in 2027. These studies are underway or starting, so there are no results to report yet. We’ll publish them, whatever they show.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q09": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do you pronounce MUTO?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO is pronounced “MEW-toe”. It’s Latin for “transform”.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
