    "faqs_what_to_expect": {
      "type": "custom-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_q10": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How long does MUTO take to work?",
            "content": "<p>Give MUTO 60 to 90 days, taken daily, before you judge it. Some customers say they notice a difference in their energy or recovery within the first few weeks; others notice nothing early on. If you track on a wearable, read it as 30-day averages, not single nights. That’s why our guarantee runs for 90 days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q11": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will MUTO give me an energy boost?",
            "content": "<p>No, not the kind you feel within an hour. Caffeine and energy drinks borrow energy and it resets every morning. MUTO supplies nutrients your body uses to make energy, including vitamins B6, B12 and folate, which contribute to the reduction of tiredness and fatigue.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q12": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How do I track whether MUTO is working?",
            "content": "<p>Note your starting point before your first dose, give it 90 days, then compare. There are two ways to do it.</p><p><strong>Without a wearable:</strong> once a week, rate your energy, sleep, afternoons and mood out of 10. It takes 30 seconds, and writing it down turns a feeling into a record you can look back on.</p><p><strong>With a wearable:</strong> note your 7-day averages for HRV, resting heart rate and recovery, then compare 30-day averages, not single nights.</p><p>Either way, keep the rest of your routine steady and check in on days 30, 60 and 90. Then it’s your call. If you don’t see a difference, you’re covered.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q13": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Do I need a wearable?",
            "content": "<p>No. A wearable makes tracking easier, but a 30-second weekly check-in (energy, sleep, afternoons and mood, each out of 10) works too. Felt changes are easy to forget, so writing them down is what turns a feeling into a record you can look back on.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q14": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What if I don’t notice a difference?",
            "content": "<p>Then you’re covered. Email us and we’ll help you check consistency, timing and anything else that might be masking a change. If you still don’t see a difference by day 90, we’ll refund you under the 90-day guarantee.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q15": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Will MUTO improve my HRV?",
            "content": "<p>We don’t promise what any number will do. Bodies vary, and HRV is affected by sleep, stress, training and illness. What we offer is a fair way to find out for yourself: baseline it, track the trend for 90 days, and if you don’t see a difference, we’ll refund you.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q16": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Which wearables work best for tracking?",
            "content": "<p>Any device that records HRV and resting heart rate overnight works. Garmin, WHOOP and Oura measure through the night, which gives steadier averages. Apple Watch takes fewer HRV readings, so wear it overnight with sleep tracking on and judge it on longer averages.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
