    "faqs_ingredients": {
      "type": "custom-faqs",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_q29": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What ingredients are in MUTO?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO contains 19 ingredients, every one declared at its full dose, with no proprietary blend. Per daily serving of two capsules:</p>",
            "content_html": "<table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Ingredient</th><th scope=\"col\">Form</th><th scope=\"col\">Per 2 capsules</th><th scope=\"col\">% NRV</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Vitamin D3</strong></td><td>Cholecalciferol, from algae</td><td>50µg (2,000 IU)</td><td>1000%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin K2</strong></td><td>Menaquinone-7 (MK-7)</td><td>100µg</td><td>133%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B1</strong></td><td>Thiamine</td><td>5mg</td><td>455%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B2</strong></td><td>Riboflavin</td><td>5mg</td><td>357%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B3</strong></td><td>Niacin</td><td>16mg NE</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B5</strong></td><td>Pantothenic acid</td><td>10mg</td><td>167%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B6</strong></td><td>Pyridoxal-5&#x27;-phosphate</td><td>5mg</td><td>357%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Folate</strong></td><td>Methyltetrahydrofolate</td><td>400µg</td><td>200%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Vitamin B12</strong></td><td>Methylcobalamin</td><td>100µg</td><td>4000%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Biotin</strong></td><td>—</td><td>300µg</td><td>600%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Zinc</strong></td><td>Bisglycinate</td><td>15mg</td><td>150%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Copper</strong></td><td>Bisglycinate</td><td>1mg</td><td>100%</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Trimethylglycine (TMG)</strong></td><td>Betaine anhydrous</td><td>450mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Nicotinamide riboside (NR)</strong></td><td>—</td><td>300mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Grape seed extract</strong></td><td>Vitis vinifera L., 120:1, 95% polyphenols (equivalent to 18,000mg grape seed)</td><td>150mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Coenzyme Q10</strong></td><td>Ubiquinone</td><td>150mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Trans-resveratrol</strong></td><td>—</td><td>50mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>PQQ</strong></td><td>Pyrroloquinoline quinone</td><td>20mg</td><td>†</td></tr><tr><td><strong>BioPerine®</strong></td><td>Piper nigrum L., fruit, 95% piperine</td><td>5mg</td><td>†</td></tr></tbody></table><p>NRV = nutrient reference value. † No reference intake established.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q30": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why does MUTO use NR?",
            "content": "<p>MUTO uses NR because it’s one of the most studied NAD+ precursors and is authorised for use in food supplements in Great Britain, at up to 300mg a day for adults. MUTO contains exactly 300mg. In a published clinical study, 300mg of NR a day raised blood NAD+ by 51% after 14 days (Conze et al., <em>Scientific Reports</em>, 2019). That study tested NR on its own, not MUTO.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q31": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What’s the difference between NR and NMN?",
            "content": "<p>NR and NMN are both NAD+ precursors: compounds your body converts into NAD+ by slightly different routes. NR is authorised for food supplements in Great Britain; NMN is currently under novel food assessment. MUTO uses NR so every ingredient in the core formula is on the right side of UK rules.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q32": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Why not just take NR on its own?",
            "content": "<p>You can, but NR alone covers one input. MUTO pairs it with nutrients that have authorised roles in how your body makes and uses energy: B vitamins and copper for normal energy-yielding metabolism, and zinc for protecting cells from oxidative stress. It also adds CoQ10, TMG, resveratrol and PQQ. One routine instead of several separate products.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q33": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can MUTO replace some of my other supplements?",
            "content": "<p>Possibly. MUTO contains full doses of nutrients many people already buy separately: a methylated B complex, zinc, copper, vitamin D3 (2,000 IU), vitamin K2, CoQ10 and an NR product. Compare your current labels against ours before stopping anything, and check with your GP before changing anything you take for a medical reason.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q34": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MUTO contain caffeine or stimulants?",
            "content": "<p>No. MUTO contains no caffeine and no stimulants. It isn’t designed to give you a buzz. It supplies nutrients your cells use every day, which is why it works alongside your morning coffee rather than replacing it.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_q35": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MUTO vegan?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. MUTO is vegan: the capsules are made from HPMC, a plant cellulose, and the vitamin D3 comes from algae. It contains no major allergens and no fillers.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
